# DTF tier manifest: scan-grading-os-and-jar
#   (artifact-keeper#5236, #5262, #5170, #5628; all fixed on main for 1.12.0;
#   only #5262 is also on the 1.11.x line)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a run-time-filled upstream (upstreams.mock-files,
# a stdlib-python server on 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files the oracle writes
# over a control API). fixtures/build_fixtures.py builds an Alpine v3.22
# branch, a Debian bookworm suite, a RHEL 9 yum tree and a Maven repository
# with fixed timestamps; the oracle stores them in the mock. LOCAL-ONLY:
# verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded DB
# (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# THE BUGS
# #5236  An Alpine subpackage is graded through a synthetic installed record
#        naming its origin; grype's NVD CPE search for the origin rewrote the
#        subpackage CPE (libcurl:libcurl -> curl:curl), which NVD does not use
#        (haxx:curl). libcurl 8.14.1-r4 graded clean (0 findings) and passed a
#        fail_closed gate that blocks curl 8.14.1-r4. Since #5726 the origin
#        is cataloged as itself and its findings are folded onto the
#        subpackage.
# #5262  A JAR was scanned as a directory, so syft's POM cataloger read the
#        embedded META-INF/maven/.../pom.xml and cataloged its declared
#        dependencies, `provided` and `test` scope included: a Maven plugin was
#        blocked for maven-core's CVEs. Since #5340 directory scans exclude
#        the embedded build POMs; pom.properties still name the archive and
#        each bundled component.
# #5170  (items 1 and 2) A Debian version marker naming another release than
#        the suite (+deb11u1 in a Debian 12 suite) was not cross-checked, and
#        a pool file no cached index lists was graded on the one release every
#        cached suite agreed on. Since #5228 both are inconclusive (423 under
#        fail_closed). Item 3 (signed .apk metadata in
#        AlpineHandler::extract_pkginfo) feeds FormatHandler::parse_metadata,
#        which no HTTP route reaches; the backend's unit tests cover it.
# #5628  A proxy rescan has no request, so it cannot pin a .deb / .rpm to its
#        release: it catalogs the package itself and matches nothing. Before
#        #5711 that clean, unpinned result replaced the release-pinned
#        vulnerable verdict (200 {"state":"clean"}). Now it is refused with
#        503 RESCAN_REQUEST_PINNED and the verdict and pin are kept.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on a main image before all four fixes (sha-5458c71; 1.11.13
#              has no Debian/RPM/Alpine scan-on-proxy and carries #5262), GREEN
#              on main:
#              #5236 libcurl 8.14.1-r4 on v3.22: 403 scan_blocked, >= 10
#                    findings;
#              #5262 the plugin JAR: 200 X-AK-Scan: clean, verdict clean;
#              #5170 dtf-oldmark 1.0-1+deb11u1 (listed in bookworm) and
#                    dtf-unlisted 1.0-1 (listed nowhere): 423
#                    scan_identity_unestablished, no verdict;
#              #5628 rescan of the openssl .deb and openssl-libs .rpm: 503
#                    RESCAN_REQUEST_PINNED, verdict vulnerable and pin kept,
#                    the next pull still 403.
#   (CONTROL)  hold on BOTH images: the unscanned Remote streams every .deb;
#              curl 8.14.1-r4, log4j-core 2.14.1, openssl ~deb12u2 and
#              openssl-libs el9_2 are 403 scan_blocked; an unmarked .deb the
#              bookworm index lists is 200 clean.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: requests back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
COVERS="5236 5262 5170 5628"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
